{"advance_requested_at_utc":"2026-10-11T15:32:11.864458+00:00","confirmed_proved":true,"job_id":"9f4c6bec-2c25-4692-bf22-d85cf6f9df94","last_publish_verdict":{"body":{"created_at":"2026-10-11T15:32:16.334665+00:00","definitions":"import Mathlib.Tactic\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_InterpolationMatrix_CoreData\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_MatrixArithmetic_CoreData\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_DeterminantContradiction_CoreData\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_MatrixArithmetic_ScalesCosts\nimport Theorems.Thm_OAI_PiExponent_InterpolationMatrix_entry_truncatedLog_cleared_gaussian\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.MatrixArithmetic\nopen scoped BigOperators\n\n","error_message":"","formal_statement":"theorem OAI.PiExponent.MatrixArithmetic.selectedMinor_clearing_bound {m K : ℕ} {w0 v0 θ F H : ℝ}\r\n    (p : Fin m → ℤ) (q : Fin m → ℕ) (hq : ∀ i, 2 ≤ q i) (hw0 : 0 < w0)\r\n    (selection : InterpolationMatrix.Row K v0 θ (logWeights q) H →\r\n      InterpolationMatrix.Column w0 (logWeights q) H)\r\n    (hdet : (selectedMinor K w0 v0 θ F H p q selection).det ≠ 0) :\r\n    -(Fintype.card (InterpolationMatrix.Row K v0 θ (logWeights q) H) : ℝ) *\r\n      Real.log (denominator q (truncationOrders q F v0) H) -\r\n      columnCost q selection + rowCost K v0 θ q H ≤\r\n      Real.log ‖(selectedMinor K w0 v0 θ F H p q selection).det‖ := by\n  sorry\n","id":"9f4c6bec-2c25-4692-bf22-d85cf6f9df94","kind":"problem","natural_language_statement":"For the original truncated-logarithm interpolation matrix, choose a square minor with nonzero determinant. Under the stated positive integer denominator and weight assumptions, its logarithmic determinant is bounded below by the negative row-count times the logarithm of the common denominator, minus the selected column cost, plus the row cost. The definitions and indices are exactly those of the source theorem.\n\nHere $m,K\\in\\mathbb{N}$; $w_0,v_0,\\theta,F,H\\in\\mathbb{R}$; $p:\\operatorname{Fin}(m)\\to\\mathbb{Z}$; $q:\\operatorname{Fin}(m)\\to\\mathbb{N}$ with $q_i\\ge 2$; $w_0>0$; and the selection maps the source row index set to the source column index set.  If the selected minor $M_{\\mathrm{sel}}$ has nonzero determinant, then, with $r$ its row count, $D$ the source common denominator, and $C_{\\mathrm{col}},C_{\\mathrm{row}}$ the source column and row costs,\n\n$$-r\\log D-C_{\\mathrm{col}}+C_{\\mathrm{row}}\\leq\\log\\lVert\\det M_{\\mathrm{sel}}\\rVert.$$","source":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/MatrixArithmetic.lean#L337-L358","status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["number-theory","linear-algebra","openai-pi-exponent-017"],"theorem_id":"922467c8-68a8-4256-9a01-ee896d0f153e","theorem_name":"OAI.PiExponent.MatrixArithmetic.selectedMinor_clearing_bound","theorem_title":"A denominator-clearing lower bound for a selected interpolation minor","updated_at":"2026-10-11T15:35:25.709388+00:00","visibility":"public"},"http_status":200},"last_verify_verdict":{"body":{"created_at":"2026-10-11T15:38:15.129625+00:00","error_message":"","file_path":"922467c8-68a8-4256-9a01-ee896d0f153e/418b0711-62a5-416a-ba5d-876ae8758fe3/ba0472e2-99f9-4e59-ad19-c38d47fb1669.lean","id":"ba0472e2-99f9-4e59-ad19-c38d47fb1669","status":"ACCEPTED","theorem_id":"922467c8-68a8-4256-9a01-ee896d0f153e","updated_at":"2026-10-11T15:41:40.514564+00:00","user_id":"418b0711-62a5-416a-ba5d-876ae8758fe3"},"http_status":200},"preparation":{"API_used":false,"actual_external_instance_reference_differences":{"OAI.PiExponent.Arithmetic.cleared_det_norm_bound":{"fields":["valueRefs","allUsedConstants"],"generated_only":["CStarAlgebra.toNormedRing","CommCStarAlgebra.toCStarAlgebra","CommCStarAlgebra.toNormedCommRing","instCommCStarAlgebraComplex"],"source_only":["NormedCommRing.toNormedRing","NormedField.toNormedCommRing